WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.740
A child's toy car is
stuck on a level crossing.

2
00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:05.910
A train comes round a bend.

3
00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:08.880
The driver faints, for medical reasons.

4
00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:11.370
The brakes apply automatically.

5
00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:14.420
The train stops a few feet from the child.

6
00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:16.450
The mother thanks God.

7
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:19.600
Yet every step has a natural explanation.

8
00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:21.850
No law of nature is broken.

9
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:26.110
So can an event with ordinary
causes still be a miracle?

10
00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:29.980
In this mission, you'll meet four
rival definitions of miracle,

11
00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.330
starting with Aquinas and Hume.

12
00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:35.430
Then you'll sort their
answers with two questions:

13
00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:39.410
what kind of event is it,
and what makes it a miracle?

14
00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:44.180
Your mission: find out whether an event
with natural causes can still count as

15
00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:45.010
a miracle.
